-all-that-glitters-is-gold-tracking-copperdragons-sparrow-framework-around-the-globe/\">Not All That Glitters Is Gold: Tracking CopperDragon’s Sparrow Framework Around the Globe</a>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><a href=\"https://www.infostealers.com/article/remus-stealer-markets-persistent-gmail-access-hudson-rock-investigates/\">Remus Stealer Markets Persistent Gmail Access: Hudson Rock Investigates</a>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><a href=\"https://www.huntress.com/blog/sckit-worm-rogue-screenconnect\">SCKit Worm Installs Rogue ScreenConnect Clients and Session Cookie Relays Across Hundreds of Endpoints</a>&nbsp;</p><p><a href=\"https://www.irpimedia.eu/en/spied-on-by-governments-with-israeli-spyware-in-europe-no-one-pays-the-price/\">Spied on by governments with Israeli spyware: in Europe, no one pays the price</a></p><p><a href=\"https://www.infostealers.com/article/school-bomb-threats-hudson-rock-finds-reported-sender-accounts-in-infostealer-data/\">School Bomb Threats: Hudson Rock Finds Reported Sender Accounts in Infostealer Data</a>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><a href=\"https://blackpointcyber.com/blog/screenconnect-attack-sckit/\">ScreenConnect Attack: SCKit Turns Remote Support Into an Attack Platform</a>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><a href=\"https://safedep.io/blog/github-actions-wfx-credential-stealer\">wfx: GitHub Actions Credential Stealer Hits 8,000 Repos</a></p><p><a href=\"https://www.justice.gov/opa/pr/gootloader-malware-disrupted-international-cyber-operation\">Gootloader Malware Disrupted in International Cyber Operation</a>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><a href=\"https://research.intezer.com/blog/2026/11/when-everything-becomes-open-source/\">When Everything Becomes Open-Source</a>&nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p><a href=\"https://blog.malwaremustdie.org/2026/11/mmd-072-2026-artex-detection-signature.html\">MMD-072-2026 – ARTEX detection signature pack – from IOC w/playbook process</a>&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><a href=\"https://www.enea.com/insights/the-enemy-within-tracking-liminal-panda-and-silentair-through-mobile-networks/\">The Enemy Within. Tracking LIMINAL PANDA and SilentAir through Mobile Networks</a></p><p><a href=\"https://www.mdpi.com/2076-3417/16/22/11266\">Ensemble Learning for Android Malware Detection: Stability Across Malware Categories and Feature Representations</a></p><p><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.08608\">AutoPYara: Next-Gen YARA Rule Generator for Malware Family Clustering</a></p><p><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.03774\">What Malware Actually Does: An Empirical Analysis of Post-Infection Behavior Across Malware Families</a></p><p><a href=\"https://cursor.com/blog/security-incident-update\">Cursor An update on our recent security incident</a></p><p><a href=\"https://www.ledger.com/blog-response-hardware-implant-attack\">Ledger’s Response to the Hardware Implant Attack</a>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Follow me on Twitter:&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://twitter.com/securityaffairs\"><strong>@securityaffairs</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/sec.affairs\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://infosec.exchange/@securityaffairs\"><strong>Mastodon</strong></a><strong></strong></p><p><a href=\"http://www.linkedin.com/pub/pierluigi-paganini/b/742/559\"><strong>Pierluigi&nbsp;Paganini</strong></a><strong></strong></p><p><strong>(</strong><a href=\"http://securityaffairs.co/wordpress/\"><strong>SecurityAffairs</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;–&nbsp;hacking,&nbsp;<a href=\"https://securityaffairs.com/tag/newsletter\">newsletter</a>)</strong></p>","zhKind","complete","汇总","漏洞分析","蓝队","检测工程","工具发布","https://securityaffairs.com/203156/malware/security-affairs-malware-newsletter-round-123.html","Security Affairs",{"_91":92,"_93":-5},"changelogVersion","2026-10-01T08:00","release"]
